The '''Progress Party''' ({{Langx|ca|Partit Progressista}}; {{Langx|oc|Partit del Progrès}}) was a political party that governed [[Cerdanya]] throughout the later 19th century and early 20th century (1872–1919). It was ideologically aligned with [[W:Fiscal conservatism|fiscal conservatism]] or [[W:Classical liberalism|classical liberalism]], and was widely known to employ [[W:Political machine|political machine]] tactics and the [[W:Spoils system|spoils system]] to maintain political power.

The Progress Party was ousted from power during the [[Baliscan Revolution]] in which many of its leading members were arrested and, in the most egregious cases, [[W:Lynching|lynched]], after which their wealth was expropriated. This prompted a large number of those aligned with the Party to flee the country, often to [[Potocsí]], [[Balboa]], or [[Lacashe]]. The Progress Party continued as a {{W|rump party}} amidst the revolutionary fervor, but was forcefully dissolved in the lead-up to the [[1919 Confederal Convention]]. 

